[left][center][font=Arial][size=6][color=#FCEE0A][b]CONFLICT STUDIO[/b][/color][/size][/font]
[color=#00F0FF]Archive and code conflict evidence for Cyberpunk 2077[/color]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qcargile/Cyberpunk-Conflict-Studio/main/docs/nexus/media/00-overview.gif[/img]
[/center]
[line]

[font=Arial][size=5][color=#FCEE0A][b]▍ CREDITS[/b][/color][/size][/font]

[font=Arial]Conflict Studio was inspired by [b]rfuzzo's[/b] [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/11126]Archive Conflict Checker[/url]. Please endorse the original tool. Conflict Studio is a separate implementation and does not copy its code or assets.[/font]
[line]

[font=Arial][size=5][color=#FCEE0A][b]▍ BETA[/b][/color][/size][/font]

[font=Arial]This is a beta.[/font]

[font=Arial]The application is unsigned and self-contained. Windows may show an unknown-publisher warning. Download it only from Nexus Mods or the linked GitHub release. A SHA-256 checksum is available alongside the ZIP on GitHub.[/font]
[line]

[font=Arial][size=5][color=#FCEE0A][b]▍ WHAT IT DOES[/b][/color][/size][/font]
[list]
[*][font=Arial]Reads the active MO2 or Vortex profile, or a manually selected game folder.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]Shows archive winners, losers, identical files, and unresolved order problems.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]Finds loose files installed by more than one active mod and shows the deployed owner.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]Inspects RedScript methods, literal CET callbacks, TweakXL changes, REDmods, and ArchiveXL manifests.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]Previews archive-order changes before Apply.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]Backs up and verifies modlist.txt, rescans, and offers Undo.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]Exports a privacy-filtered support report.[/font][/*]
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qcargile/Cyberpunk-Conflict-Studio/main/docs/nexus/media/01-overview.png[/img]

[font=Arial]Turn on [b]Show non-conflicting files[/b] to inspect unique files alongside overlaps. [b]Only in conflicting archives[/b] keeps that expanded view inside archives that have an overlap.[/font]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qcargile/Cyberpunk-Conflict-Studio/main/docs/nexus/media/17-conflicting-archives.png[/img]
[line]

[font=Arial][size=5][color=#FCEE0A][b]▍ HOW TO READ CODE RESULTS[/b][/color][/size][/font]
[list]
[*][font=Arial][b]Confirmed conflicts[/b] means active changes cannot coexist for the specific target. It does not mean the whole mods are incompatible.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial][b]Needs review[/b] means one specific question remains unanswered. The card tells you what to check.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial][b]Identical overlaps[/b] shows the same loose file or the same replacement source. It does not prove the mods are compatible elsewhere.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial][b]One deployed file is selected[/b] proves file ownership. It does not prove the selected file is the version you intended.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial][b]Different values assigned[/b] proves that active sources assign different values. It does not prove the final in-game value without a runtime observation.[/font][/*]
[/list]

[font=Arial]The detail card explains what the source shows, why Conflict Studio showed it, what it does not prove, the mods involved, and what to do.[/font]

[font=Arial]The [b]Files involved[/b] column lists the filenames. Select a finding to see each file's location on disk, open the file, show it in its folder, or copy its path.[/font]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qcargile/Cyberpunk-Conflict-Studio/main/docs/nexus/media/14-code-interactions.png[/img]

[font=Arial][b]View code[/b] opens the exact recorded operations behind a code finding and highlights the relevant source. You can switch between the operations involved and expand the surrounding context. File-ownership rows that show one installed copy taking priority use [b]Files involved[/b] instead.[/font]

[font=Arial]This comparison shows code requesting a value of 8 while another mod declares 0 for the same field.[/font]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qcargile/Cyberpunk-Conflict-Studio/main/docs/nexus/media/15-source-comparison.png[/img]

[font=Arial]This array comparison shows one source adding an entry while another removes it.[/font]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qcargile/Cyberpunk-Conflict-Studio/main/docs/nexus/media/16-array-comparison.png[/img]

[font=Arial]Use [b]Reviewed[/b] to revisit findings you have already decided for this profile. Reviews are stored at [b]%LOCALAPPDATA%\Cyberpunk Conflict Studio\decisions\evidence-decisions.json[/b] and nothing is uploaded automatically. A support bundle you choose to export can include your review notes.[/font]
[line]

[font=Arial][size=5][color=#FCEE0A][b]▍ VORTEX SETUP[/b][/color][/size][/font]
[spoiler]
[list=1]
[*][font=Arial]Click on the Home icon and open Extensions.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]Drop the downloaded ZIP onto the extension installer.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]Restart Vortex, activate your Cyberpunk profile, and deploy it.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]Launch Conflict Studio from Cyberpunk 2077 → Tools.[/font][/*]
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qcargile/Cyberpunk-Conflict-Studio/main/docs/nexus/media/11-vortex-extensions-navigation.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qcargile/Cyberpunk-Conflict-Studio/main/docs/nexus/media/12-vortex-extension-enabled.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qcargile/Cyberpunk-Conflict-Studio/main/docs/nexus/media/13-vortex-tool-launch.png[/img][/spoiler]
[line]

[font=Arial][size=5][color=#FCEE0A][b]▍ MOD ORGANIZER 2 SETUP[/b][/color][/size][/font]
[spoiler]
[list=1]
[*][font=Arial]Extract the ZIP outside the instance's mods folder.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]Add ConflictStudio.exe from the extracted folder to MO2's executable list.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]Set Start in to the folder containing ModOrganizer.ini.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]Use [b]--manager mo2 --profile current[/b] as the arguments.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]Add ConflictStudio.exe to Settings → Workarounds → Executables Blacklist.[/font][/*]
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qcargile/Cyberpunk-Conflict-Studio/main/docs/nexus/media/08-mo2-tool-setup.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qcargile/Cyberpunk-Conflict-Studio/main/docs/nexus/media/09-mo2-settings-navigation.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qcargile/Cyberpunk-Conflict-Studio/main/docs/nexus/media/10-mo2-blacklist.png[/img][/spoiler]
[line]

[font=Arial][size=5][color=#FCEE0A][b]▍ IMPORTANT[/b][/color][/size][/font]
[list]
[*][font=Arial]Do not scan the same game through MO2 while Vortex files are deployed. Purge Vortex first or use the Vortex profile.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]Cyberpunk must be closed before archive-order writes. MO2 or Vortex may remain open.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]Conflict Studio does not merge archives, generate patches, or automatically sort mods.[/font][/*]
[/list]

[font=Arial]The first large-profile scan can take longer. Later scans reuse unchanged analysis. If something looks wrong, reproduce it once and copy the report from the Support tab.[/font]
[line]

[font=Arial][size=5][color=#FCEE0A][b]▍ REQUIREMENTS[/b][/color][/size][/font]
[list]
[*][font=Arial]A Cyberpunk 2077 installation[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]Windows 10 version 20H1 (19041) or later, 64-bit[/font][/*]
[/list]

[font=Arial]No separate .NET installation or Cyberpunk framework dependency is required.[/font][/left]
